# OpenRA: Red Alert, Tiberian Dawn and Dune 2000 on a rebuilt engine,
# compiled from source with dotnet-sdk. The game data isn't included;
# the game downloads it or copies it from the original discs on first run.
#
# The projects target net6.0. The SDK builds them against the net6.0
# reference packs from NuGet, and RollForward=Major lets the result run
# on the installed .NET 10 runtime. The chroot has no network, so every
# NuGet package the solution restores (found by restoring OpenRA.sln on
# a networked host with an empty package cache, test projects included)
# is a source below; build() puts them in a local feed and a NuGet.Config
# in the source tree clears every other package source.
#
# The engine links the system's SDL2 (sdl2-compat), OpenAL (openal-soft),
# Lua 5.1 (lua51) and FreeType: configure-system-libraries.sh, run by
# make, symlinks them into bin/. HttpClient (server list, map downloads)
# needs dotnet-sdk's DOTNET_OPENSSL_VERSION_OVERRIDE for OpenSSL 4.
#
# The Makefile's own install target publishes self-contained for
# TARGETPLATFORM as a runtime identifier, and unix-generic isn't one, so
# the assemblies are copied from bin/ here and the rest (data, launchers,
# desktop files, icons, appdata, man page) uses upstream's install
# functions and targets. The IP2Location country database is left out:
# it is a monthly download with no fixed release, and the server shows
# no country flags without it
